s","Hiking"],mustDo:"Gothic Quarter (El Call) Walk",description:"A dazzling seaside metropolis combining Gaudi’s surrealist architecture, beautiful Mediterranean beaches, and a resurrected medieval Jewish quarter.",bestTimeToVisit:"May to June and September to October",nearestAirport:"Barcelona-El Prat Airport (BCN)",airportDistance:"9 miles",attractions:[{name:"El Call (Jewish Quarter)",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/wm/3f8a1f37e4744def.webp",description:"The atmospheric, narrow stone lanes of medieval Barcelona's Jewish enclave."},{name:"Park Guell",description:"A colorful, whimsical hilltop park offering sweeping ocean and city views."}],activities:[{name:"Barceloneta Beach stroll",description:"Walk or cycle along the lively boardwalk by the golden Mediterranean waves."},{name:"Montserrat Mountain Day Trip",description:"Hike among spectacular multi-peaked pink clay rock needles high above Catalonia."}],hotels:[{name:"Majestic Hotel & Spa",description:"A highly elegant neoclassical luxury hotel on the Passeig de Gracia.",price:"$$$$$"},{name:"Lamaro Hotel (formerly Hotel Colón)",description:"A fantastic, comfortable hotel directly facing Barcelona’s historic Cathedral.",price:"$$$"}],restaurants:[],transportation:"Barcelona’s TMB metro and bus network is clean, air-conditioned, super fast, and cheap.",nearby:["Montserrat","Girona (Kabbalah Center)","Costa Brava"],kosherRestaurants:[],chabad:[{name:"Chabad of Barcelona",address:"Carrer del Montnegre 14, 08029 Barcelona",rabbi:"Rabbi David Libersohn",phone:"+34 934 100 685",website:"https://jabad.barcelona/",shabbatMeals:!0,photo:""}],synagogues:[{name:"Synagogue of Barcelona (CIB)",address:"Carrer de l'Avenir 24",nusach:"Sephardic"}],eruvInfo:"Barcelona does not have a public eruv. Consult the local Rabbinical authority regarding specific hotel surroundings."},{id:"nassau",name:"Nassau",image:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/wm/baacd2f319b8ac52.webp",country:"Bahamas",region:"Caribbean",flightTimes:{"New York":"3h 10m",Miami:"0h 55m",Jerusalem:"14h 45m",Paris:"9h 30m",London:"8h 45m"},weather:"☀️ 83°F",experiences:["Beaches","Waterfalls","Wildlife"],mustDo:"Strolling the pristine shores of Cable Beach & visiting Blue Lagoon",description:"The beautiful tropical capital of the Bahamas, offering colonial charm, breathtaking coral reefs, and a highly active, welcoming Chabad House providing fresh gourmet kosher catering.",bestTimeToVisit:"mid-December to mid-April",nearestAirport:"Lynden Pindling International Airport (NAS)",airportDistance:"10 miles",attractions:[{name:"Cable Beach",description:"Wide public beach on the northern coast of New Providence Island, about 6 miles west of downtown Nassau, with soft sand and calm, clear turquoise water. Upscale resorts line the beach, and chairs, umbrellas and water sports are available."},{name:"Queen’s Staircase",description:"Historic 66-step landmark carved by hand out of solid limestone."},{name:"Blue Lagoon Island",description:"Stunning private island paradise offering tranquil lagoons and ocean adventures."}],activities:[{name:"Snorkeling at Clifton Heritage Park",description:"Explore majestic underwater sculpture gardens and thriving marine life."},{name:"Climbing the Queen’s Staircase",description:"Take a historic walk up the lush, shaded canyon steps."}],hotels:[{name:"The Cove at Atlantis",description:"Ultra-luxury oasis offering spectacular suites, private pools, and pristine ocean views.",price:"$$$$$",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/d2-the-cove-at-atlantis.webp"},{name:"Baha Mar Grand Hyatt",description:"Spectacular, massive family-friendly resort on Cable Beach.",price:"$$$$",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/baha-mar-grand-hyatt-nassau.webp"}],restaurants:[{name:"Knosh (kosher dairy food truck, Grand Hyatt Baha Mar)",description:"Fresh, gourmet kosher meals delivered directly to your resort.",kosher:!0}],transportation:"Taxis are highly available and metered. Jitney public buses offer a fun and very inexpensive local commute.",nearby:["Paradise Island","Rose Island","Exuma Cays"],chabad:[{name:"Chabad of the Bahamas",address:"446 West Bay St, Nassau, Bahamas",rabbi:"Rabbi Sholom Bluming",phone:"+1 (242) 424-4277",website:"https://www.jewishbahamas.com",shabbatMeals:!0}],kosherRestaurants:[{name:"Cinkō Asian Latino Grill (Grand Hyatt Baha Mar)",website:"https://www.cinkobahamar.com",address:"Grand Hyatt Baha Mar, West Tower lobby, 1 Baha Mar Blvd, Nassau",kashrus:"Chabad of the Bahamas (Glatt Meat / Pas Yisroel)",phone:"+1 (242) 424-4277",photo:"/defaults/chabad.webp"}]},{id:"san-juan",name:"San Juan",country:"Puerto Rico",region:"Caribbean",image:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/wm/8f9ad355f84a8416.webp",flightTimes:{"New York":"3h 50m","Westchester (HPN)":"3h 35m",Miami:"2h 30m","Fort Lauderdale":"2h 35m",Jerusalem:"15h 10m",Paris:"9h 45m",London:"9h 00m"},weather:"☀️ 84°F",experiences:["Beaches","Hiking","National Parks","Wildlife","Historic Forts","Bioluminescence","Natural Waterslides"],mustDo:"Exploring Castillo San Felipe del Morro, sliding down El Yunque natural waterslides, wading in La Posita de Piñones, and joining Shabbat in Isla Verde with Chabad",description:"A dynamic tropical capital blending 500 years of Spanish colonial history, 16th-century fortress ramparts, tranquil reef-protected lagoons, and palm-fringed Isla Verde sands. Features an active Eruv, Glatt kosher restaurant (OMRKT), Chabad library and market, and immediate access to El Yunque National Forest.",bestTimeToVisit:"December to April",nearestAirport:"Luis Muñoz Marín International Airport (SJU)",airportDistance:"3 miles to Isla Verde / 8 miles to Old San Juan",attractions:[{name:"Castillo San Felipe del Morro (El Morro)",description:"6-level 16th-century Spanish fortification standing 140 feet above the Atlantic shoreline at the entrance to San Juan Bay, in the Old San Juan historic district."},{name:"Old San Juan (Viejo San Juan)",description:"Atmospheric 500-year-old walled city paved with blue cobblestones (adoquines), featuring pastel colonial townhouses, historic plazas, the narrowest house (La Casa Estrecha), and roaming roosters."},{name:"Castillo San Cristóbal",description:"The largest European fortification built in the Americas, with labyrinthine tunnels, coastal batteries, and sweeping views of the Atlantic coast and modern San Juan ($10 NPS entrance)."},{name:"Terraplén La Posita de Piñones",description:"A natural rock pool beach in Piñones, Loíza, where a coral rock wall shelters a calm, shallow area of clear water from Atlantic waves. Popular with families and located right on Route 187, about 15 minutes from San Juan."},{name:"El Yunque Natural Waterslides (Las Paylas / Charco Frío)",description:"Natural smooth rock waterslides carved by a mountain river, with refreshing pools, a rope swing, and optional cliff jumps near Luquillo."},{name:"El Yunque National Forest (Yokahú & Britton Towers)",description:"The only tropical rainforest in the US National Forest System, featuring misty mountain ridges, Juan Diego Falls cascades, and panoramic stone lookout towers."},{name:"Isla Verde Beach",description:"Expansive crescent of golden sand and turquoise waves running parallel to the residential and resort strip, featuring plane-spotting views of landing aircraft."},{name:"La Casa Estrecha (Narrowest House)",description:"Bright yellow two-story house in Old San Juan, only about 5 feet wide and wedged between two standard-size buildings. It was once an alleyway that was converted into a home.",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/wm/6994f5874b95b262.webp"}],activities:[{name:"La Posita de Piñones Lagoon & Boardwalk Walk",description:"Wade in a crystal-clear, wave-free natural saltwater pool protected by a coral reef wall, hunt for sea shells, and stroll along the oceanfront Piñones boardwalk."},{name:"El Yunque Natural Waterslide & River Trek",description:"Hike wet, slippery rainforest trails near El Yunque to natural rock waterslides, cliff jumps, and a rope swing into cool mountain pools."},{name:"Old San Juan GPS Audio Walking Tour",description:"Take a self-guided smartphone GPS audio tour through historic fortifications, colorful La Perla neighborhood viewpoints, and 500-year-old Spanish bastions."},{name:"El Yunque Rainforest Waterfall Hike",description:"Hike through lush emerald canopy trails to Yokahú Tower, Mount Britton, and the refreshing mountain pools of Juan Diego Falls."},{name:"Bioluminescent Bay Night Kayak Tour",description:"Paddle under dark moonless skies through mangrove channels into Laguna Grande in Fajardo or catch an excursion to Vieques’ famous Mosquito Bay."},{name:"Isla Verde Beach & Plane Spotting Walk",description:"Relax on the palm-lined beach within the Isla Verde Eruv, or take an afternoon walk along the airport perimeter, a popular spot for plane spotting near SJU airport."}],hotels:[{name:"Residence Inn by Marriott San Juan Isla Verde",description:"All-suite hotel located on Avenida Isla Verde, offering spacious units with full kitchens, a swimming pool with water playground and slides, and convenient on-site amenities.",price:"$$$",address:"6500 Isla Verde Ave, Carolina, PR 00979",phone:"+1 (787) 961-1155",website:"https://www.marriott.com/en-us/hotels/sjuri-residence-inn-san-juan-isla-verde/overview/",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/wm/e5da85bc5795c307.webp",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"About 0.4 km (5-minute walk) from Chabad of Puerto Rico, 18 Calle Rosa, whose Kosher in Paradise sells kosher food. All suites have full kitchens. Pueblo supermarket is about 0.4 km away. Chabad runs an Isla Verde eruv; ask Chabad whether the hotel is inside it."},{name:"Fairmont El San Juan Hotel",description:"Iconic historic landmark on Isla Verde Beach blending 1960s timeless glamour with modern luxury, featuring a hand-carved mahogany lobby, crystal chandelier, sprawling multi-pool sanctuaries, and spacious guest rooms with private balconies.",price:"$$$$",address:"6063 Av. Isla Verde, Carolina, 00979, Puerto Rico",phone:"+1 (787) 791-1000",website:"https://www.fairmont.com/el-san-juan-hotel/",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/fairmont-el-san-juan-hotel.webp",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"About 0.3 km (a few minutes' walk) from Chabad of Puerto Rico, 18 Calle Rosa, whose Kosher in Paradise sells kosher food and Shabbat essentials. Chabad lists the hotel. Rooms have a mini-refrigerator. Chabad runs an Isla Verde eruv; ask whether the hotel is inside it."},{name:"Hampton Inn & Suites San Juan",description:"Comfortable, highly accommodating hotel located in the heart of Isla Verde, within easy walking distance to the beach and Chabad, offering complimentary breakfast and daily poolside drinks.",price:"$$",address:"6530 Av. Isla Verde, Carolina, 00979, Puerto Rico",phone:"+1 (787) 791-8777",website:"https://www.hilton.com/en/hotels/sjuhshx-hampton-suites-san-juan/",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/hampton-inn-suites-san-juan-san-juan.webp",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"About 0.35 km (5-minute walk) from Chabad of Puerto Rico, 18 Calle Rosa. Rooms have a refrigerator; hot breakfast is free and guests get beach chairs and umbrellas. Chabad runs an Isla Verde eruv; ask whether the hotel is inside it."},{name:"Four Seasons Resort and Residences Puerto Rico",description:"Exquisite 5-star ultra-luxury eco-resort nestled between El Yunque National Forest and a 2-mile secluded beach in Río Grande, offering private estate rooms with jungle paths and soothing rainforest sounds.",price:"$$$$$",address:"State Road 187 Kilometer 4.2, Río Grande, 00745, Puerto Rico",phone:"+1 (787) 809-8000",website:"https://www.marriott.com/en-us/hotels/sjuxr-the-st-regis-bahia-beach-resort-puerto-rico/overview/",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/d2-the-st-regis-bahia-beach-resort-puerto-rico.webp",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"Set on a former coconut farm near El Yunque. Rooms have a wet bar and refrigerator. About 21 km from Chabad in Isla Verde, so not walkable to Chabad or the eruv; best for weekdays."},{name:"The Ritz-Carlton, San Juan",description:"Prestigious beachfront luxury resort on Isla Verde Beach, offering palatial Caribbean elegance, fine dining, a grand pool complex, and lavish oceanfront cabanas.",price:"$$$$$",address:"6961 Av. Los Gobernadores, Carolina, 00979, Puerto Rico",phone:"+1 (787) 253-1700",website:"https://www.ritzcarlton.com/en/hotels/sjurz-the-ritz-carlton-san-juan/overview/",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/d4-ritz-carlton-san-juan.webp",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"About 0.35 km (5-minute walk) from Chabad of Puerto Rico, 18 Calle Rosa, on Isla Verde Beach. Chabad runs an Isla Verde eruv; ask whether the hotel is inside it."},{name:"Marriott Isla Verde Beach Resort",description:"Energetic oceanfront resort in Isla Verde featuring direct beach access, outdoor hammocks under coconut palms, beachfront dining, and quick 5-minute proximity to SJU airport.",price:"$$$",address:"7012 Boca de Cangrejos Beach Trail, Carolina, 00979, Puerto Rico",phone:"+1 (787) 791-0404",website:"https://www.marriott.com/en-us/hotels/sjuiv-courtyard-isla-verde-beach-resort/overview/",photo:"",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"About 0.9 km (roughly a 12-minute walk) from Chabad of Puerto Rico. Rooms have a mini fridge."},{name:"Condado Vanderbilt Hotel",description:"Legendary 1919 Spanish Revival oceanfront luxury resort in the exclusive Condado district, featuring Michelin-caliber dining, cascading coastal pools, and lavish oceanfront suites.",price:"$$$$$",address:"1055 Ashford Ave, San Juan, 00907, Puerto Rico",phone:"+1 (787) 721-5500",website:"https://www.condadovanderbilt.com",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/wm/459cc6b46583fc37.webp",photos:["https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/wm/459cc6b46583fc37.webp"],kosherFriendlyNotes:"About 0.8 km from Shaare Zedeck synagogue (JCC of Puerto Rico) and OMRKT kosher restaurant in Miramar. Chabad in Isla Verde is about 7 km away. All rooms have a mini-refrigerator. Chabad of Puerto Rico lists the hotel."},{name:"Caribe Hilton",description:"Iconic 17-acre oceanfront resort on a private San Juan peninsula near historic Old San Juan, featuring secluded ocean swimming lagoons, tropical gardens, and oceanfront pools.",price:"$$$$",address:"1 C. San Gerónimo, San Juan, 00901, Puerto Rico",phone:"+1 (787) 721-0303",website:"https://www.caribehilton.com",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/wm/203d256347bbafc0.webp",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"On a 17-acre oceanfront peninsula between Old San Juan and Condado. Rooms have mini refrigerators. OMRKT kosher restaurant in Miramar is about 1.5 km away; Chabad in Isla Verde is about 8 km."}],restaurants:[{name:"OMRKT Kosher Restaurant",type:"Glatt Meat / Israeli Grill",kosher:!0,description:"The premier certified Glatt Kosher restaurant in Puerto Rico (located in Miramar), featuring indoor and outdoor patio dining. Menu includes savory pumpkin soup, ribeye steaks, schnitzel, chicken, salmon, falafel, house-made lo mein, fried rice, salads, fruit smoothies, and specialty cocktails. Offers Shabbat takeout packages under Chabad rabbinical supervision."}],transportation:"Ubers and taxis are readily available throughout San Juan. Note that Uber wait times can reach 10-15 minutes with occasional driver cancellations during busy periods. Airport taxi insider tip: Walking across to the airport parking garage taxi stand offers flat ~$16 fares to Isla Verde (avoiding peak $35 Uber arrival surge rates and $25 curb solicitations). When renting a car at SJU for day trips to El Yunque and Ceiba, request an electronic toll transponder (toll roads PR-66 and PR-52 are all-electronic cashless plazas). Off-peak Ubers around Isla Verde and to SJU often cost under $5.",travelTips:["January Yeshivah Week Surge Warning: Puerto Rico’s Jewish infrastructure experiences heavy demand during the annual two-week January Yeshivah Week period. Chabad Shabbat meals frequently sell out completely weeks in advance (they often erect an outdoor overflow tent), and OMRKT can have lines down the block with hour-plus waits or run out of food by late evening. If visiting in January, reserve Chabad Shabbat meals well ahead of time, arrive early at OMRKT, or bring hotel cooking appliances.","Westchester (HPN) Flight Alternative: For travelers originating in Monsey, Rockland County, Westchester, or northern NJ, JetBlue flights from Westchester County Airport (HPN) to SJU offer a serene, relaxed alternative to JFK or Newark, featuring swift security lines and hassle-free boarding.","La Posita de Piñones Natural Tidal Lagoon: Located just 5-10 minutes east of Isla Verde. While the main Piñones road consists of non-kosher street kiosks, Terraplén La Posita de Piñones is an absolute hidden paradise: an ancient offshore barrier reef breaks violent ocean waves, creating a calm, shallow, crystal-clear natural swimming pool where water trickles gently over rocks. Ideal for relaxed swimming, hunting shells, and strolling the shaded oceanfront boardwalk.","El Yunque Natural Waterslides (Las Paylas / Charco Frío): For active adventurers, guided trips lead through bamboo groves to natural granite waterslides, river rope swings, and cliff jumps. Don’t worry if you didn’t pack water shoes—a local stand right at the mucky parking lot entrance sells inexpensive water shoes, waterproof phone pouches, and river gear directly on-site.","Travel Heating Devices (HotLogic Mini & Panini Grills): Packing a compact HotLogic mini portable oven allows slow, safe heating of frozen double-wrapped kosher meals (e.g. MealMart) right in your hotel room over several hours without burning or kitchen hassles. A compact panini press / sandwich grill is also ideal for warming par-baked baguettes, pizza bagels, and grilled cheese.","SJU Airport Departure USDA Agricultural Scan: When departing SJU for the US mainland, all checked luggage and carry-on bags must pass through a mandatory USDA agricultural inspection scanner before entering airline check-in lines or TSA security checkpoints. Allow an extra 15-20 minutes at the airport for this routine scan.","Old San Juan Museum Schedules & Audio Tours: Most historic museums in Old San Juan are closed on Mondays and Tuesdays (operating Wednesday through Sunday). Self-guided GPS audio apps (like Action Tour Guides) are an excellent fallback, providing detailed historical narration walking from the cruise docks past Castillo San Cristóbal, El Morro, and the colorful La Perla seaside enclave.","The Perfect Puerto Rico Split-Stay: For frum travelers, a winning itinerary is spending Thursday to Sunday in Isla Verde (Fairmont El San Juan, Residence Inn, or Hampton Inn), near the eruv (confirm with Chabad whether your hotel is inside it) and a short stroll to Chabad for Shabbat prayers and community dinners. On Sunday, transition east to The St. Regis Bahia Beach in Río Grande for serene rainforest luxury, tranquil beach pools, and immediate access to El Yunque and eastern excursions.","El Yunque Next-Day Ticket Drop: If vehicle passes or trail permits appear sold out weeks in advance on recreation.gov, don’t panic: the US Forest Service releases a major batch of next-day tickets every morning at 8:00 AM AST the day prior to entry. Set an alarm to snag your reservation easily.","Mainland Bio Bay (Laguna Grande / Fajardo) vs. Vieques (Mosquito Bay): Travelers should weigh expectations carefully. While Laguna Grande in Fajardo is an easy drive from San Juan, the kayak tour requires navigating narrow mangrove grass channels against stiff currents on the paddle back, mosquitoes can be fierce, and water glow is often very dim. For the true bucket-list electric-blue glow, make the trip to Mosquito Bay in Vieques (the world’s brightest biobay) and time it during the moonless nights of Rosh Chodesh.","Balcony Prep & Sunset Grilling: If staying at beachfront properties like Fairmont El San Juan, rooms feature balconies suitable for well-ventilated travel cooking with compact electric appliances. Additionally, public coastal parks around San Juan offer breathtaking sunset spots for grilling dinners with portable disposable grills.","SJU Airport Arrivals & Taxi Hack: When multiple flights land simultaneously at SJU, Uber activates surge pricing (climbing from $8 to $35), while curbside taxi drivers often solicit $25. Walk across to the official airport parking garage taxi stand where standard regulated fares to Isla Verde run ~$16. When returning off-peak to SJU, an Uber can cost as little as $4.","TSA & Frozen Kosher Liquids: You can pack frozen Cholov Yisroel milk bottles and cheeses through TSA security checkpoints without checking bags, provided they are frozen solid when passing the scanner. Using a small personal-item cooler bag alongside backpacks allows a seamless carry-on trip.","Supermarket Provisions & Betty Crocker Cooking: Pueblo Supermarket in Isla Verde is within easy walking distance of the Residence Inn and Chabad, stocking kosher-certified wraps, eggs, pizza sauce, smoked salmon, pareve cookies, ices, and potatoes. Bringing a mini-Betty Crocker electric skillet/pizza maker allows quick hotel-room prep of hot meals, grilled wraps, and potato kugel.","Local Canned Sodas & Kashrus Vigilance: Unlike US mainland stores where brands like Schweppes or Gatorade are universally certified, local Puerto Rican bottling plants produce versions without kosher certification logos. Always check the physical can/bottle for a reliable kosher symbol before purchasing.","Old San Juan Walking & Parking Logistics: Municipal parking lots (e.g. near the port or Paseo Covadonga) cost only ~$5 for the day. Explore early in the morning or late in the afternoon, as midday Caribbean sun and humidity can be intense. Bacardi Rum Factory tours cost ~$40/person and require travel across the bay—skippable unless you are a committed rum aficionado.","El Yunque National Forest Practicalities: The drive is ~45 minutes east of San Juan. Drive directly onto Highway PR-191 to access Yokahú Tower, Mount Britton, and Juan Diego Falls. Caution: Parking is strictly enforced in designated bays only; rangers issue steep $150 tickets for parking on non-designated road shoulders. The trail climb behind Juan Diego Falls can be extremely slick and dangerous when wet. Applying mosquito patches or repellent ensures a completely bug-free rainforest hike."],nearby:["Dorado Beach","Vieques Island","El Yunque Rainforest","Fajardo Laguna Grande","Culebra Flamenco Beach","Ponce"],chabad:[{name:"Chabad Jewish Center of Puerto Rico (Isla Verde Campus)",address:"18 Calle Rosa, Carolina, PR 00979 (Isla Verde)",rabbi:"Rabbi Mendel Zarchi & Rabbi Levi Zarchi",phone:"(787) 253-0894",website:"https://www.jewishpuertorico.com",shabbatMeals:!0,photo:"/defaults/chabad.webp",photos:[]},{name:"Jewish Welcome Center of Old San Juan (Chabad)",address:"Old San Juan Historic District (Calle San Justo / Cruise Port Hub), San Juan, PR 00901",rabbi:"Rabbi Levi Zarchi & Mrs. Mushkie Zarchi",phone:"+1 (787) 253-0770",website:"https://www.jewishpuertorico.com",shabbatMeals:!1,photo:"/defaults/chabad.webp",photos:[]},{name:"Chabad Dorado (Chabad Villa Dorado)",address:"Dorado Beach / Chabad Villa Dorado, Dorado, PR 00646",rabbi:"Rabbi Mendel Zarchi & Rabbi Levi Zarchi",phone:"(787) 253-0894",website:"https://www.jewishpuertorico.com/templates/articlecco_cdo/aid/6683485/",shabbatMeals:!0,photo:"/defaults/chabad.webp",photos:[]}],synagogues:[{name:"Shaare Zedeck Synagogue (JCC of Puerto Rico)",address:"903 Ponce de León Ave, Miramar, San Juan, 00907",nusach:"Traditional / Ashkenaz & Sephardic",phone:"(787) 724-4157",website:"https://www.jccpr.org",description:"Founded in 1953, Shaare Zedeck is the premier historic traditional congregation in Puerto Rico. Featuring a stately sanctuary, daily morning Shacharit minyan, Shabbat morning services with communal kiddush, and full kosher catering kitchen.",photo:"/defaults/shul.webp",photos:[]},{name:"Temple Beth Shalom (San Juan)",address:"101 Calle San Jorge, San Juan, 00911",nusach:"Liberal / Egalitarian",phone:"+1 (787) 721-6333",website:"https://tbspr.org",description:"San Juan Reform congregation serving English and Spanish speaking members and visitors, with Friday night Shabbat services and community celebrations."}],mikvah:{name:"Mikvah Chabad of Puerto Rico",address:"18 Calle Rosa, Carolina, PR 00979 (Inside Chabad Center)",photo:"/defaults/shul.webp"},kosherRestaurants:[{name:"OMRKT Kosher Restaurant",address:"Miramar Plaza, 954 Ave Juan Ponce de León Suite 101, San Juan, PR 00907",kashrus:"Caribbean Kosher / Chabad of Puerto Rico (Rabbi Mendel Zarchi - Glatt Meat / Pas Yisroel)",phone:"(787) 333-0123",website:"https://kosheromrkt.com",distance:"Inside Isla Verde Jewish Center",type:"Glatt Kosher Steakhouse & Israeli Grill",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/d2-omkrt-orchid-meat-kosher-restaurant-kosher-in-paradise.webp"}],kosherGroceries:[{name:"The Kosher Pantry at Chabad",address:"18 Calle Rosa, Carolina, 00979 (Chabad Isla Verde)"},{name:"Pueblo Supermarket (Isla Verde)",address:"Av. Los Gobernadores, Carolina, PR 00979 (Isla Verde)"}],eruvInfo:"Isla Verde has an eruv run by Chabad of Puerto Rico. The boundary ends at Begonia Street (south of it is outside). Ask Chabad whether your hotel is inside before Shabbat; status and map at jewishpuertorico.com."},{id:"vieques-island",name:"Vieques Island",country:"Puerto Rico",region:"Caribbean",flightTimes:{"New York":"4h 30m (via SJU/Ceiba)",Miami:"3h 10m (via SJU/Ceiba)","Fort Lauderdale":"3h 15m",Jerusalem:"16h 00m",Paris:"10h 30m",London:"9h 45m"},weather:"☀️ 85°F",experiences:["Bioluminescence","Beaches","Wildlife","Kayaking","Off-Road Adventures"],mustDo:"Night kayaking in Mosquito Bay (world’s brightest bioluminescent bay) under a moonless sky and exploring Black Sand Beach",description:"An unspoiled, laid-back Caribbean island sanctuary off Puerto Rico’s eastern coast. Home to an estimated 1,000–3,000 free-roaming wild Spanish horses, dramatic black sand beaches, and Mosquito Bay—officially recognized by Guinness World Records as the brightest bioluminescent bay on Earth.",bestTimeToVisit:"December to May (Plan tours around Rosh Chodesh / New Moon for peak darkness)",nearestAirport:"Antonio Rivera Rodríguez Airport (VQS) / Ceiba Airport (NRR)",airportDistance:"10-minute flight from Ceiba Airport",attractions:[{name:"Mosquito Bay (Puerto Mosquito Bio Bay)",description:"Bahía Bioluminiscente (Puerto Mosquito Bio Bay) in Vieques is famed as one of the brightest bioluminescent bays in the world. Paddling disturbs Pyrodinium bahamense dinoflagellates, making the water glow blue, best experienced on a guided kayak tour at night."},{name:"Black Sand Beach (Playa Negra)",description:"Small pocket beach on the south coast of Vieques near Esperanza, where magnetic black volcanic sand streaks the golden shoreline, backed by sandy cliffs and desert-like bushes. Swimming can be dangerous here.",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/wm/fef8c8d4e88947aa.webp"},{name:"Sun Bay Beach (Sombe)",description:"Vast, crescent-shaped public beach with tranquil turquoise waters, soft white sand, and coconut palm groves."},{name:"Wild Paso Fino Horses of Vieques",description:"Descendants of horses left by 16th-century Spanish settlers, roughly 2,000 Paso Fino horses roam freely along roadsides, pastures, and beaches across Vieques."}],activities:[{name:"Clear Kayak Bioluminescent Tour",description:"Paddle a transparent two-person kayak into Mosquito Bay on moonless nights, watching electric blue light burst beneath the hull and sparkle across your hands."},{name:"Trail Walk to Playa Negra (Black Sand Beach)",description:"A walk of about half a mile (roughly 15-20 minutes) along a trail off PR-997 through a lush, jungle-like tropical riverbed, leading down to Playa Negra, a secluded black sand beach. Wear shoes, as the trail has many roots."},{name:"UTV or Jeep Island Discovery",description:"Drive a Jeep Wrangler or open-air UTV across quiet unpaved coastal tracks to deserted coves and snorkeling reefs."}],hotels:[{name:"El Blok Hotel",description:"Adults only (18+). Celebrated architectural boutique hotel on the Esperanza Malecón in Vieques, featuring sculpted curvilinear concrete design, rooftop plunge pool, and panoramic Caribbean sunset views.",price:"$$$",address:"158 Calle Flamboyan, Vieques, 00765, Puerto Rico",phone:"+1 (787) 741-6020",website:"https://elblok.com",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/el-blok-hotel-vieques-island.webp",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"Across the street from the beach on Esperanza's Malecón, close to biobay tour meeting points. Rooms have a mini-fridge. The hotel describes its rooms as an adults-only escape."}],restaurants:[{name:"Self-Catering & San Juan Chabad Provisions",type:"Self-Catered / Pack-In Kosher",kosher:!0,description:"There are no certified kosher restaurants on Vieques Island. Travelers should order packaged takeout from OMRKT / Chabad of Puerto Rico in San Juan or carry shelf-stable meal kits."}],transportation:"Ferry vs Air: Ferries from Ceiba to Vieques are bumpy, sell out rapidly on weekends, and their return schedule does not allow for post-dark biobay tours. The recommended route is flying with Vieques Air Link from Ceiba Airport (NRR) to Vieques (VQS), a 10-minute flight. On the island, rent a Jeep or an open-air UTV.",travelTips:["The Frum Advantage — Rosh Chodesh & Biobay Darkness: The bioluminescence of Mosquito Bay is best witnessed on moonless nights; moonlight washes out the neon glow. Because the Jewish calendar is strictly lunar, traveling around Rosh Chodesh (the beginning/end of the Hebrew month) guarantees pitch-black skies and the brightest possible dinoflagellate fire.","Ceiba to Vieques 10-Minute Flight: Skip the crowded, nausea-inducing Ceiba ferry. Drive to Ceiba Airport (NRR - José Aponte de la Torre Airport), park right outside the small terminal building, and take the 10-minute Vieques Air Link flight. Arrive ~20 minutes before departure for check-in.","Clear Kayak Night Tour Gear: Book with reputable clear-kayak operators (like Alikei Adventures). Wear water sandals/shoes and quick-drying shorts, as water continually splashes into the kayak as you paddle. Cameras and smartphones cannot capture the bioluminescent light without specialized long-exposure equipment, so immerse yourself in the live sensory experience of dipping your hands to watch sparks of light dance across your skin.","Wild Horses of Vieques: Be alert while driving around the island! An estimated 1,000–3,000 Spanish Paso Fino horses roam completely wild across road shoulders, trails, and beaches.","Kosher Food Prep: Vieques has no certified kosher dining or Chabad center. Pick up Glatt kosher meals, sandwiches, and Shabbat packages from OMRKT / Chabad in San Juan before flying over, or bring shelf-stable tuna, wraps, and cheese."],nearby:["San Juan","El Yunque Rainforest","Fajardo","Culebra Island"],chabad:[{name:"Chabad Jewish Center of Puerto Rico",address:"18 Calle Rosa, Carolina, PR 00979 (Isla Verde / SJU Airport)",rabbi:"Rabbi Mendel Zarchi & Rabbi Levi Zarchi",phone:"(787) 253-0894",website:"https://www.jewishpuertorico.com",shabbatMeals:!0,photo:"/defaults/chabad.webp"}]},{id:"dorado-beach",name:"Dorado Beach",country:"Puerto Rico",region:"Caribbean",flightTimes:{"New York":"3h 50m (to SJU) + 35m drive",Miami:"2h 30m (to SJU) + 35m drive","Fort Lauderdale":"2h 35m (to SJU) + 35m drive",Jerusalem:"15h 30m",Paris:"10h 15m",London:"9h 30m"},weather:"☀️ 84°F",experiences:["Luxury Resorts","Beaches","Golf","Biking Trails","Fine Dining","Nature Reserves"],mustDo:"Exploring the 11-mile Rockefeller nature trail by golf cart, lounging at Dorado Beach, and spending an unforgettable Shabbat at Chabad Villa Dorado",description:"An exclusive Caribbean coastal sanctuary located 20 miles west of San Juan. Renowned for its storied history as a Rockefeller family eco-estate, Dorado Beach offers pristine crescent coral lagoons, world-class championship golf courses, private luxury villas, and a blossoming Jewish presence centered around Chabad Villa Dorado.",bestTimeToVisit:"December to May",nearestAirport:"Luis Muñoz Marín International Airport (SJU)",airportDistance:"22 miles (approx. 35-45 minutes by highway)",attractions:[{name:"Dorado Beach & Rockefeller Nature Trail",description:"Historic 11-mile Rockefeller Nature Trail winding through forests and beaches at Dorado Beach, a Ritz-Carlton Reserve resort."},{name:"East & Sugarcane Golf Courses",description:"Seaside golf courses at TPC Dorado Beach, with ocean views and coconut palm groves."},{name:"Balneario Manuel Morales (Dorado Beach Public Park)",description:"Public beach (balneario) in Dorado, also known as Playa Sardinera, with calm surf, a roped-off swimming area, lifeguards, restrooms, showers, gated parking, and shaded picnic and grilling areas."},{name:"Ojo del Buey (Ox Eye Park)",description:"Coastal promontory in Dorado where the Río La Plata meets the Atlantic, marked by a large rock formation resembling an ox head."}],activities:[{name:"Private Golf Cart Cruising",description:"Navigate miles of car-free lush jungle paths connecting luxury residences, lagoons, and private beach clubs."},{name:"Lagoon Paddleboarding & Kayaking",description:"Paddle across the calm, reef-protected waters of Condado Lagoon in San Juan, with occasional manatee sightings possible."},{name:"Spa Botanico Treehouse Massage",description:"Five-acre spa at Dorado Beach, a Ritz-Carlton Reserve, offering massages, facials, scrubs and wraps made with local Puerto Rican ingredients. Massages can be booked on one of two outdoor treehouse platforms."}],hotels:[{name:"Dorado Beach, a Ritz-Carlton Reserve",description:"Ultra-exclusive 5-star sanctuary nestled within 1,400 acres of natural sanctuary, featuring private plunge pools, open-air outdoor showers, dedicated Embajador butler service, and direct beach frontage.",price:"$$$$$",address:"100 Dorado Beach Drive, Dorado, 00646, Puerto Rico",phone:"+1 (787) 626-1100",website:"https://www.ritzcarlton.com/en/hotels/sjudo-dorado-beach-a-ritz-carlton-reserve/overview/",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/dorado-beach-a-ritz-carlton-reserve-dorado-beach.webp",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"Chabad of Puerto Rico lists the resort with a 10% discount for its guests. Some ground-floor suites open onto the beach. About 30 km from Chabad in Isla Verde; not walkable for Shabbat."},{name:"Plantation Resort Residences at Dorado Beach",description:"Spacious three- and four-bedroom luxury condominiums with gourmet kitchens, expansive verandas, golf course views, and access to all Dorado Beach Resort amenities.",price:"$$$$",address:"500 Plantation Dr, Suite 1, Dorado, PR 00646",phone:"+1 (787) 626-1001",website:"https://www.doradobeachresidences.com",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/plantation-resort-residences-at-dorado-beach-dorado-beach.webp",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"Residences have full gourmet kitchens; villa listings show Sub-Zero refrigerators."},{name:"Embassy Suites by Hilton Dorado del Mar Beach Resort",description:"Vibrant family beach resort nestled within the Dorado del Mar gated community, featuring spacious two-room suites with kitchenettes, free made-to-order breakfast, and lagoon pools.",price:"$$$",address:"201 Dorado Del Mar Blvd, Dorado, 00646, Puerto Rico",phone:"+1 (787) 796-6125",website:"https://www.hilton.com/en/hotels/dorpr-embassy-suites-dorado-del-mar-beach-resort/",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/embassy-suites-by-hilton-dorado-del-mar-beach-resort-dorado-beach.webp",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"Every suite has a microwave, refrigerator and wet bar."}],restaurants:[{name:"Chabad Villa Dorado Shabbat Meals & Kosher Delivery",type:"Glatt Kosher Catering & Shabbat Hospitality",kosher:!0,description:"Chabad of Puerto Rico operates Chabad Villa Dorado in Dorado Beach, coordinating minyanim, community Shabbat hospitality, and fresh delivery of Glatt kosher dinners, lunches, and meat platters from OMRKT directly to Dorado hotels and villas."}],transportation:"Rental Car: A rental car from SJU airport is recommended for the 35-40 minute drive along Highway PR-22 to Dorado. Inside the Dorado Beach resort gates, private golf carts and bicycles are the preferred and ubiquitous mode of transportation along the Rockefeller nature trail.",travelTips:["Shabbat in Dorado Beach: Contact Chabad of Puerto Rico (787-253-0894 / jewishpuertorico.com) well in advance of your trip to confirm minyan times, Shabbat meals, and kosher catering delivery to Dorado Beach villas.","Kosher Provisions: Order frozen or prepared Glatt kosher meats, wine, grape juice, and challah from The Pantry @ Chabad in Isla Verde on your way from SJU airport before heading west to Dorado.","Golf Cart Living: Nearly all estate homes and resort suites at Dorado Beach include private golf carts to explore the beaches, fitness wellness centers, and nature reserve paths."],nearby:["San Juan","El Yunque Rainforest","Arecibo Observatory & Caves","Cerro Gordo Beach"],chabad:[{name:"Chabad Dorado (Chabad Villa Dorado)",address:"Dorado Beach / Chabad Villa Dorado, Dorado, PR 00646",rabbi:"Rabbi Mendel Zarchi & Rabbi Levi Zarchi",phone:"(787) 253-0894",website:"https://www.jewishpuertorico.com/templates/articlecco_cdo/aid/6683485/",shabbatMeals:!0,photo:"/defaults/chabad.webp",photos:[]},{name:"Chabad Jewish Center of Puerto Rico (Main Campus)",address:"18 Calle Rosa, Carolina, PR 00979 (Isla Verde)",rabbi:"Rabbi Mendel Zarchi & Rabbi Levi Zarchi",phone:"(787) 253-0894",website:"https://www.jewishpuertorico.com",shabbatMeals:!0,photo:"/defaults/chabad.webp"}],kosherRestaurants:[{name:"OMRKT Kosher Restaurant (delivers)",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/d2-omkrt-orchid-meat-kosher-restaurant-kosher-in-paradise.webp",address:"954 Ave Juan Ponce de León Suite 101, Miramar, San Juan, PR 00907",kashrus:"Caribbean Kosher / Chabad of Puerto Rico (Rabbi Mendel Zarchi)",phone:"(787) 333-0123",website:"https://kosheromrkt.com",distance:"Delivery directly to Dorado Beach resort residences and villas",type:"Glatt Kosher Catering, Grill & Shabbat Meals"}]},{id:"palm-beach",name:"Palm Beach",country:"Aruba",region:"Caribbean",image:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/wm/4969de218166848a.webp",flightTimes:{"New York":"4h 30m",Miami:"2h 50m","Fort Lauderdale":"2h 55m",Boston:"4h 50m",Jerusalem:"16h 00m",Paris:"10h 45m",London:"10h 00m"},weather:"☀️ 85°F",experiences:["Beaches","Glatt Kosher Dining","Water Sports","Desert Safaris","Luxury Resorts","Snorkeling & Diving","Family & Shabbat Getaways"],mustDo:"Savoring a Glatt Kosher dinner at Piccolo Italian Steakhouse at the Hyatt Regency, spending Shabbat with Chabad of Aruba, snorkeling with sea turtles at Tres Trapi Beach at sunset, and exploring the Butterfly Farm with family",description:"A sun-drenched Dutch Caribbean paradise famous for turquoise waters, powder-soft sands, reliable cooling trade winds, and world-class hospitality. Located safely outside the Caribbean hurricane belt, Aruba offers exceptional year-round sunny weather, premier beachfront luxury resorts, spacious family villas, and a vibrant kosher travel ecosystem featuring multiple on-island Glatt kosher dining options and an active Chabad Jewish Center.",bestTimeToVisit:"Year-round (warm and dry; high season is mid-December to mid-April)",nearestAirport:"Queen Beatrix International Airport (AUA)",airportDistance:"6 miles (approx. 15-20 min drive)",attractions:[{name:"Tres Trapi Beach & Malmok Boardwalk",description:"A small cove in Aruba with limestone steps leading into calm, clear water, known for snorkeling, sea turtles, and natural caves carved into the limestone."},{name:"Arashi Beach",description:"Picturesque beach with shallow, calm water and excellent shore-entry snorkeling where kids and families can observe schools of colorful fish."},{name:"The Butterfly Farm Aruba",description:"Tropical garden enclosure near Palm Beach housing exotic free-flying butterflies, with guided tours for all ages."},{name:"Palm Beach High-Rise Strip",description:"Two-mile strip of white-sand beach on Aruba's west coast, lined with high-rise resorts and restaurants, with water sports concessions and calm waters good for swimming."},{name:"Arikok National Park & Conchi Natural Pool",description:"Protected desert reserve covering nearly 20% of Aruba, with rugged volcanic cliffs, hidden caves, and the Conchi natural pool encircled by volcanic rock formations and protected from the sea by surrounding rocks."},{name:"California Lighthouse & Dunes",description:"Historic lighthouse built 1914–1916 on a limestone plateau near Arashi Beach and the Sasariwichi dunes, offering 360-degree views of Aruba's coastline; visitors can climb its spiral staircase to the top."}],activities:[{name:"Atlantis Submarine / Undersea Expedition",description:"Descend 130 feet beneath the Caribbean surface aboard a real submarine to view vibrant marine life and coral reefs off Aruba's coast."},{name:"Private Boat Charter & Snorkeling Cruise",description:"Private boat and catamaran charters in the Palm Beach area take groups out along Aruba's coast for snorkeling trips."},{name:"UTV / 4x4 Rugged Desert Safari",description:"Guided off-road UTV/4x4 tour across Aruba's rugged desert terrain along the northern coastline."},{name:"Kitesurfing & Windsurfing at Fisherman's Huts",description:"Popular windsurfing and kitesurfing spot on Palm Beach with shallow, flat, sandy water and steady side-shore trade winds, suited for both beginners and experienced riders."}],hotels:[{name:"Bocobay Porta al Sole Condos & Townhomes",description:"Upscale modern residential community located around the corner from Chabad of Aruba on Salina Cerca. Features multi-bedroom townhomes with full chef kitchens, community pool, and private rooftop terraces ideal for relaxing family stays and outdoor Shabbat meals.",price:"$$$$",address:"Bakval 8, Noord, Aruba",phone:"",website:"",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/bocobay-porta-al-sole-condos-townhomes-palm-beach.webp",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"About 0.2 km (2-minute walk) from Chabad of Aruba on Salina Cerca. Townhomes have full kitchens, and listed units have rooftop terraces and a BBQ."},{name:"The Ritz-Carlton, Aruba",description:"Five-star beachfront sanctuary at the serene northern end of Palm Beach, featuring private oceanfront balconies and swimming pools.",price:"$$$$$",address:"L.G. Smith Blvd 107, Noord, Aruba",phone:"+297 527 2222",website:"https://www.ritzcarlton.com/en/hotels/auart-the-ritz-carlton-aruba/overview/?scid=f2ae0541-1279-4f24-b197-a979c79310b0",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/the-ritz-carlton-aruba-palm-beach.webp",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"About 0.5 km (roughly an 8-minute walk) from Chabad of Aruba on Salina Cerca. Marriott says rooms have no fridge, so ask before booking."},{name:"Radisson Blu Aruba",description:"Modern upscale boutique suites resort in Palm Beach featuring 2-bedroom and 3-bedroom suites with expansive living spaces and full kitchenettes, rooftop infinity pool, and family pools.",price:"$$$",address:"J.E. Irausquin Blvd 97-A, Noord, Aruba",phone:"+297 526 5000",website:"https://www.choicehotels.com/aruba/palm-beach/radisson-blu-hotels/aw007?mc=llgoxxpx",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/d2-radisson-blu-aruba.webp",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"Under 1 km (about a 10-minute walk) from Chabad of Aruba. Two-bedroom suites have a kitchenette with refrigerator; three-bedroom suites have a full kitchen with a full-size fridge."},{name:"Courtyard by Marriott Aruba Resort",description:"Comfortable resort nestled near Palm Beach, featuring lush courtyard pools, family suites with kitchenettes, and convenient access to island attractions.",price:"$$$",address:"J.E. Irausquin Blvd 330, Noord, Aruba",phone:"+297 586 7700",website:"https://www.marriott.com/en-us/hotels/auacy-courtyard-aruba-resort/overview/?scid=f2ae0541-1279-4f24-b197-a979c79310b0",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/courtyard-by-marriott-aruba-resort-palm-beach.webp",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"Rooms have a microwave and mini-fridge. About 2 km from Chabad of Aruba."},{name:"Ocean Z Boutique Hotel",description:"Intimate and tranquil 5-star boutique hotel nestled in the Noord / Malmok area directly across from Caribbean sunset shores. Featuring designer oceanfront suites with private swim-out infinity pools and personalized five-star hospitality.",price:"$$$$",address:"L.G. Smith Blvd 526, Noord, Aruba",phone:"+297 586 9500",website:"http://oceanzaruba.com/",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/ocean-z-boutique-hotel-palm-beach.webp",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"About 2.5 km from Chabad of Aruba (taxi on weekdays; a long walk for Shabbat)."},{name:"Boardwalk Boutique Hotel Aruba",description:"Charming private Caribbean casitas nestled in a historic coconut grove steps from Palm Beach, each equipped with private barbecue patios and modern full kitchens ideal for kosher family cooking.",price:"$$$",address:"Bakval 20, Noord, Aruba",phone:"+297 586 6654",website:"https://www.boardwalkaruba.com/en?utm_source=google&utm_medium=organic&utm_campaign=gmb",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/boardwalk-boutique-hotel-aruba-palm-beach.webp",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"Every casita has a private patio and BBQ grill, with kitchenette or full-kitchen options. About 0.4 km (5-minute walk) from Chabad of Aruba."}],restaurants:[{name:"Piccolo Italian Steakhouse @ Hyatt Regency Aruba",type:"Upscale Glatt Kosher Steakhouse & Italian Dining",kosher:!0,description:"Full-service fine dining Glatt Kosher restaurant at the Hyatt Regency serving prime aged steaks, handmade pasta, fresh fish, fine wines, and Friday night Shabbat dinners (reservations required via piccoloaruba.com)."},{name:"Pizzaiolo / Pizza by the Beach @ Hyatt Regency Aruba",type:"Kosher Artisanal Pizza & Beachside Cafe",kosher:!0,description:"Beachfront kosher food truck at the Hyatt Regency serving freshly baked artisanal kosher pizzas, calzones, crisp Mediterranean salads, and cold beverages."},{name:"Chabad Aruba Rimon Corner & Shabbat-in-a-Bag",type:"Glatt Kosher Market, Deli & Shabbat Hospitality",kosher:!0,description:"Depot at the Chabad Center offering frozen Glatt kosher beef, poultry, cold cuts, kosher wines, fresh challah, and full pre-ordered Shabbat dinner/lunch packages."}],transportation:"Taxis operate on government-regulated fixed flat rates between the airport, hotels, and beaches. Car or UTV rentals are highly recommended for exploring Arikok National Park, the northern coast, and Baby Beach.",travelTips:["Shabbat & Family Travel in Aruba: Chabad of Aruba hosts welcoming Shabbat dinners, uplifting tefilos, festive Friday night meals, and community Havdalah. Bocobay Porta al Sole Condos (right around the corner) feature private rooftop terraces ideal for relaxing family meals.",'Shabbat in Aruba: Make advance reservations for Friday night dinner at Piccolo Italian Steakhouse (piccoloaruba.com) or book communal Shabbat meals and "Shabbat-in-a-Bag" takeout with Chabad of Aruba (jewisharuba.com).',"Walking to Chabad: Bocobay Porta al Sole is a 2-minute stroll to Chabad on Salina Cerca. High-rise hotels on Palm Beach (Hyatt Regency, Marriott, Ritz-Carlton) are a flat 15-20 minute walk.","Best Snorkeling & Sunsets: Head to Tres Trapi Beach for natural limestone carved steps, sea turtles, and jaw-dropping golden hour sunsets, and Arashi Beach for shallow family-friendly fish feeding.",`Family Attractions: Don't miss the Aruba Butterfly Farm near Palm Beach and the Atlantis Submarine dive for an unforgettable live undersea "aquarium" experience.`,"Self-Catering & Bringing Food: For travelers bringing home-cooked meals, boutique hotels like Ocean Z in Malmok are exceptionally kosher-friendly—offering double-wrapped food warming, large refrigerators, and raw uncut produce/eggs. Packing a travel mini-griddle or electric pan makes hot breakfasts (pancakes, omelets) effortless.","Sun & Wind: Aruba's pleasant trade winds mask strong UV radiation (12°N latitude). Use broad-spectrum reef-safe sunscreen and stay hydrated."],nearby:["Oranjestad","Eagle Beach","Arikok National Park","California Dunes","San Nicolas & Baby Beach"],chabad:[{name:"Chabad Jewish Center of Aruba",photo:"/defaults/chabad.webp",address:"Salina Cerca 31C, Noord, Aruba",rabbi:"Rabbi Ahron Blasberg & Rebbetzin Chani Blasberg",phone:"+297 592 7613",website:"https://www.jewisharuba.com",shabbatMeals:!0}],synagogues:[{name:"Beth Israel Synagogue (Beth Israel Aruba)",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/wm/0ac6053c5e718368.webp",address:"Adriaan Laclé Boulevard 2, Oranjestad, Aruba",phone:"+297 582 3272",website:"https://www.bethisraelaruba.com",description:"Historic Jewish community center and synagogue of Aruba established in 1962, holding traditional Friday evening Shabbat services for residents and island visitors."}],kosherRestaurants:[{name:"Piccolo Italian Steakhouse",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/piccolo-italian-steakhouse-palm-beach.webp",address:"J.E. Irausquin Blvd 85, Palm Beach (Hyatt Regency Aruba Resort)",kashrus:"Glatt Kosher - Supervised by Rabbi Ahron Blasberg / Chabad of Aruba",phone:"+297 586 4563",website:"https://www.piccoloaruba.com",type:"Glatt Kosher Prime Steaks, Pasta & Shabbat Dinners"},{name:"Pizzaiolo (kosher food truck at Hyatt Regency Aruba)",address:"J.E. Irausquin Blvd 85, Palm Beach (Hyatt Regency Aruba Resort)",kashrus:"Kosher Dairy / Parve - Supervised by Rabbi Ahron Blasberg / Chabad of Aruba",phone:"+297 586 1234",website:"https://www.jewisharuba.com/templates/articlecco_cdo/aid/7206749/",type:"Handcrafted Kosher Pizza, Calzones & Fresh Salads"},{name:"Rimon Corner & Shabbat-in-a-Bag @ Chabad of Aruba",address:"Salina Cerca 31C, Noord, Aruba",kashrus:"Glatt Kosher / Cholov Yisroel - Chabad of Aruba",phone:"+297 592 7613",website:"https://www.jewisharuba.com",type:"Glatt Kosher Takeout, Shabbat Meals & Grocery Depot"}]},{id:"oranjestad",name:"Oranjestad",country:"Aruba",region:"Caribbean",flightTimes:{"New York":"4h 30m",Miami:"2h 50m","Fort Lauderdale":"2h 55m",Boston:"4h 50m",Jerusalem:"16h 00m",Paris:"10h 45m",London:"10h 00m"},weather:"☀️ 85°F",experiences:["Colonial Architecture","Cultural Heritage","Harbor Cruises","Beaches","Shopping"],mustDo:"Visiting Beth Israel Synagogue and the historic Jewish cemetery, strolling past pastel Dutch colonial facades on Main Street, and taking a water taxi to Renaissance Island",description:"The colorful, historic capital city of Aruba, situated on the southern coast. Oranjestad blends 18th-century Dutch colonial architecture painted in pastel hues with bustling seaside marinas, vibrant open-air tramways, duty-free boutiques, and significant Jewish cultural heritage dating back to 18th-century Sephardic merchants.",bestTimeToVisit:"Year-round (warm and dry; high season is mid-December to mid-April)",nearestAirport:"Queen Beatrix International Airport (AUA)",airportDistance:"2.5 miles (approx. 7-10 min drive)",attractions:[{photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/wm/0ac6053c5e718368.webp",name:"Beth Israel Synagogue",description:"Aruba’s historic, consecrated synagogue built in 1962 on Adriaan Laclé Boulevard, serving as the central house of worship for Sephardic and Ashkenazi families."},{name:"Old Jewish Cemetery of Aruba",description:"Small historic Jewish cemetery in Oranjestad, also called the Old Portuguese Jewish Cemetery, with a handful of old gravestones. It is linked to the Sephardic families from Curaçao who settled in Aruba in the 18th and 19th centuries."},{name:"Fort Zoutman & Willem III Tower",description:"Aruba’s oldest historic structure, built in 1798 by the Dutch military to protect the harbor, now housing the Historical Museum of Aruba.",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/wm/7814564df32b625e.webp"},{name:"Renaissance Island & Flamingo Beach",description:"Private 40-acre offshore island near Oranjestad featuring mangrove lagoons and a world-famous beach where pink flamingos roam freely."},{name:"Wilhelmina Park & Harbor Walk",description:"Seaside park in Oranjestad along the waterfront, featuring lawns and gardens with statues of Queen Wilhelmina, overlooking the harbor and cruise port."}],activities:[{name:"Heritage Walking Tour of Colonial Oranjestad",description:"Walking tour of historic downtown Oranjestad, passing Dutch colonial facades, landmarks and monuments. Guided versions take about 2.5 hours and cover around 30 sites."},{name:"Atlantis Submarine Expedition",description:"Dive 130 feet beneath the Caribbean surface in a US Coast Guard-certified passenger submarine to explore sunken coral shipwrecks."},{name:"Water Taxi to Renaissance Island",description:"Take the free water taxi from inside the Renaissance Wind Creek Aruba Resort lobby in Oranjestad for a short ride to the private Renaissance Island, home to Flamingo Beach."}],hotels:[{name:"Renaissance Wind Creek Aruba Resort",description:"Vibrant dual-zone resort featuring the adults-only Marina Hotel and family-friendly Ocean Suites with exclusive private water taxi access to Renaissance Flamingo Beach.",price:"$$$$",address:"L.G. Smith Blvd 82, Oranjestad, Aruba",phone:"+297 583 6000",website:"https://www.marriott.com/en-us/hotels/auabr-renaissance-wind-creek-aruba-resort/overview/?scid=f2ae0541-1279-4f24-b197-a979c79310b0",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/renaissance-wind-creek-aruba-resort-oranjestad.webp",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"Rooms have a mini fridge. About 0.7 km from Beth Israel Synagogue (Conservative) in Oranjestad; Chabad of Aruba is about 7 km away in Noord."}],restaurants:[{name:"Piccolo Italian Steakhouse (Palm Beach Delivery / Access)",type:"Upscale Glatt Kosher Dining",kosher:!0,description:"Located a short 10-minute taxi ride north in Palm Beach at the Hyatt Regency, offering prime Glatt kosher steaks, pastas, and Shabbat dinners."},{name:"Chabad Aruba Rimon Corner Kosher Depot",type:"Glatt Kosher Takeout & Provisions",kosher:!0,description:"Located in Noord, supplying kosher groceries, frozen Glatt meats, wine, and Shabbat meal delivery across Oranjestad hotels and villas."}],transportation:"Oranjestad features a free heritage streetcar (tram) connecting the cruise terminal through downtown shopping streets. Taxis are ubiquitous with fixed rates, and local Arubus lines connect downtown directly to Eagle Beach and Palm Beach.",travelTips:["Beth Israel Services: Visitors are warmly welcomed for Friday evening Shabbat services at Beth Israel Synagogue. Reach out in advance via bethisraelaruba.com.","Kosher Logistics: If staying in Oranjestad, arrange kosher meal pick-up or delivery with Chabad of Aruba in nearby Noord (10 min drive) or dine at Piccolo at the Hyatt Regency in Palm Beach.","Flamingo Beach Access: Day passes or reservations at Renaissance Wind Creek Resort provide exclusive access to private Renaissance Island."],nearby:["Palm Beach","Eagle Beach","Mangel Halto Reef","Arikok National Park","Queen Beatrix Airport"],synagogues:[{name:"Beth Israel Synagogue (Beth Israel Aruba)",photo:"/defaults/shul.webp",address:"Adriaan Laclé Boulevard 2, Oranjestad, Aruba",phone:"+297 582 3272",website:"https://www.bethisraelaruba.com",description:"Historic Jewish community center and synagogue of Aruba established in 1962, holding traditional Friday evening Shabbat services for residents and island visitors."}],chabad:[{name:"Chabad Jewish Center of Aruba (Noord / Palm Beach)",photo:"/defaults/chabad.webp",address:"Salina Cerca 31C, Noord, Aruba (10 min from Oranjestad)",rabbi:"Rabbi Ahron Blasberg & Rebbetzin Chani Blasberg",phone:"+297 592 7613",website:"https://www.jewisharuba.com",shabbatMeals:!0}],kosherRestaurants:[{name:"Piccolo Italian Steakhouse",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/piccolo-italian-steakhouse-palm-beach.webp",address:"J.E. Irausquin Blvd 85, Palm Beach (Hyatt Regency Aruba Resort)",kashrus:"Glatt Kosher - Supervised by Rabbi Ahron Blasberg / Chabad of Aruba",phone:"+297 586 4563",website:"https://www.piccoloaruba.com",type:"Glatt Kosher Prime Steaks & Shabbat Dinners"},{name:"Pizzaiolo (kosher food truck at Hyatt Regency Aruba)",address:"J.E. Irausquin Blvd 85, Palm Beach (Hyatt Regency Aruba Resort)",kashrus:"Kosher Dairy / Parve - Supervised by Rabbi Ahron Blasberg / Chabad of Aruba",phone:"+297 586 1234",website:"https://www.jewisharuba.com",type:"Handcrafted Kosher Pizza, Calzones & Fresh Salads"},{name:"Rimon Corner & Shabbat-in-a-Bag @ Chabad of Aruba",address:"Salina Cerca 31C, Noord, Aruba",kashrus:"Glatt Kosher / Cholov Yisroel - Chabad of Aruba",phone:"+297 592 7613",website:"https://www.jewisharuba.com",type:"Glatt Kosher Takeout, Shabbat Meals & Grocery Depot"}]},{id:"eagle-beach",name:"Eagle Beach",country:"Aruba",region:"Caribbean",flightTimes:{"New York":"4h 30m",Miami:"2h 50m","Fort Lauderdale":"2h 55m",Boston:"4h 50m",Jerusalem:"16h 00m",Paris:"10h 45m",London:"10h 00m"},weather:"☀️ 85°F",experiences:["Beaches","Tranquility","Luxury Resorts","Water Sports","Family & Shabbat Getaways"],mustDo:"Photographing the iconic fofoti trees on wide white sands at sunset, snorkeling at nearby reefs, and enjoying Glatt kosher meals delivered from Chabad of Aruba",description:"Ranked among the top beaches in the world, Eagle Beach is famous for its vast expanse of powder-soft white sand, calm turquoise waters, and iconic fofoti trees (often mistaken for divi-divi trees). Offering a quieter, more relaxed ambience than neighboring Palm Beach, it features boutique low-rise resorts with full suites and kitchens, ideal for tranquil family getaways and Shabbat stays.",bestTimeToVisit:"Year-round (warm and dry; high season is mid-December to mid-April)",nearestAirport:"Queen Beatrix International Airport (AUA)",airportDistance:"5.5 miles (approx. 12-15 min drive)",attractions:[{name:"Eagle Beach Shoreline & Fofoti Trees",description:"Aruba’s signature post-card coastline featuring the famous twisted fofoti trees leaning toward the Caribbean sea on wide white sands.",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/wm/ed436186f8bcb827.webp",photos:["https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/wm/ed436186f8bcb827.webp"]},{name:"Bubali Bird Sanctuary",description:"Protected wetland sanctuary located between Palm Beach and Eagle Beach with an observation tower overlooking marshlands home to over 80 migratory bird species.",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/wm/ef59abe45caa33fa.webp",photos:["https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/wm/ef59abe45caa33fa.webp"]}],activities:[{name:"Sunset Catamaran Cruise",description:"Glide along the serene Eagle Beach coastline at golden hour enjoying tropical ocean breezes."},{name:"Eagle Beach Sea Turtle Watching",description:"Witness protected nesting grounds and seasonal hatching of giant leatherback and green sea turtles."}],hotels:[{name:"Amsterdam Manor Beach Resort Aruba",description:"Charming Dutch colonial-style beachfront resort directly opposite world-famous Eagle Beach and the iconic fofoti trees, featuring studio and two-bedroom suites with full kitchens.",price:"$$$$",address:"J.E. Irausquin Blvd 252, Oranjestad, Aruba",phone:"+297 527 1100",website:"https://www.amsterdammanor.com/?utm_source=GMB&utm_medium=GMB&utm_campaign=GMB&utm_content=GMB&utm_term=GMB",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/amsterdam-manor-beach-resort-aruba-eagle-beach.webp",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"Every unit has a fully equipped kitchen or kitchenette, on Eagle Beach. About 3.5 km from Chabad of Aruba."},{name:"Bucuti & Tara Beach Resort",description:"Adults only (18+). Award-winning, tranquil eco-luxury oceanfront sanctuary on the widest stretch of Eagle Beach, known for peaceful atmosphere, personalized concierge service, and pristine sands.",price:"$$$$$",address:"L.G. Smith Boulevard 55B, Oranjestad, Aruba",phone:"+297 583 1100",website:"https://www.bucuti.com/?utm_medium=organic&utm_source=google&utm_campaign=business-listing",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/d2-bucuti-tara-beach-resort.webp",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"Adults-only (18+), so not for families with children. Rooms have a microwave and refrigerator. About 5 km from Chabad of Aruba."},{name:"Manchebo Beach Resort & Spa",description:"Boutique wellness resort set on Aruba’s widest stretch of white sand on Eagle Beach, featuring serene tropical gardens, yoga pavilion, and intimate oceanfront tranquility.",price:"$$$$",address:"J.E. Irausquin Blvd 55, Oranjestad, Aruba",phone:"+297 522 3444",website:"https://www.manchebo.com/?utm_source=google&utm_medium=organic&utm_campaign=business-listing",photo:"https://kosher-travel-img.sites.tab.bot/venues/manchebo-beach-resort-spa-eagle-beach.webp",photos:[],kosherFriendlyNotes:"Rooms have a mini-fridge, with a microwave on request. About 5 km from Chabad of Aruba."}],restaurants:[{name:"Chabad Aruba Kosher Meal Delivery to Eagle Beach",type:"Glatt Kosher Meal Delivery & Shabbat Packages",kosher:!0,description:"Chabad of Aruba delivers freshly prepared Glatt kosher dinners, lunches, and full Shabbat packages directly to Eagle Beach resort lobbies."},{name:"Piccolo Italian Steakhouse (Palm Beach)",type:"Upscale Glatt Kosher Dining (10 min drive)",kosher:!0,description:"Fine dining Glatt kosher steakhouse and Italian restaurant located a short 5-10 minute taxi ride awa